# Where the app talks to the Lifedeck API. EXPO_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined into
# the JS bundle at build time, so this must be a public URL — never put a secret
# here. The app authenticates with the session JWT from the keychain instead.
#
# Local development against `pnpm dev`: on the iOS simulator localhost works;
# on a physical device or the Android emulator use your machine's LAN IP
# (e.g. http://192.168.0.10:3000), because localhost is the device itself.
#
# Whatever host you point at, it must answer WITHOUT redirecting. A redirect to
# another origin drops the Authorization header (fetch does this on purpose, so
# a redirect cannot steal a credential), and every authenticated call then comes
# back 401 while the sign-in itself appears to succeed. The deployed value lives
# in eas.json per build profile and is `https://www.lifedeck.com.br`, because
# the apex answers 308 to www.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
